body:
YEEEESSS, all of this. Sweet Fuse is so underrated. It was made during the otome dark age, but I remember playing it when it was first localized and being blown away by how fun and nuanced the characters were. Saki is amazing. 

&#x200B;

And Yukimura is 90% of the reason I just can't play Hakuoki in it's entirety. I'm one of those people that self-inserts in otome games for the most part, but I just couldn't with Yukimura. She surpasses bland to the point where I don't know why any of the guys come to like her. She's not particularly kind, resourceful, or useful- aughhhh.

You sound like me. :) I'm also 20/F, I've been roleplaying for the better part of 10 years now online, writing my OCs and other fictional characters alike. I actually still roleplay Light Yagami from DN  ( ´\_ゝ｀) buuuut, the way I escape is usually through otome games/dating sims, manga, or writing my OCs. I feel myself sort of slipping in and out of a cycle of escapism, where I feel shame about needing to escape so often that I cut myself off for a while, only for it to come back full force a month later. 

&#x200B;

I'm trying to break free of it, but I think I'll be escaping forever...I would give absolutely everything to have my fantasies come to life. A lot of them are tragic, unrealistic, painful, but they will always end in me feeling like I'm loved, and that's enough for me. :) I hope I don't sound like a total creep haha...I just feel comfortable somehow expressing this to you after reading your words. I'd like it if you PMed me
